    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_spring - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_spring.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spring()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes with the Fruchterman-Reingold force-directed algorithm.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spring()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes with the Fruchterman-Reingold force-directed algorithm.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_spring()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Place the nodes with the Fruchterman-Reingold force-directed algorithm.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes with the Fruchterman-Reingold force-directed algorithm.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5777-L5919){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_spring(\n    k=None,\n    iterations=50,\n    threshold=0.0001,\n    weighted=None,\n    initial=None,\n    fixed=None,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    seed=None,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Spring layout](/assets/graphs/layout-spring.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, the cube graph (eight nodes, each joined to three others) scattered at random. On the right, layout_spring(seed=1) treats edges as springs and nodes as repelling charges, and the cube settles into one square inside another.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nNodes behave like charged particles joined by springs: every pair repels with force\n`k^2 / d` and every edge pulls its ends together with force `w * d^2 / k`, where `d`\nis their distance, `w` the edge weight and `k` the ideal edge length. Starting from\nrandom positions, each iteration moves every node along its net force by at most the\ncurrent \"temperature\", which cools linearly from a tenth of the starting area to zero,\nso the layout settles. The run stops early once the mean move falls below\n`threshold=`. The result is centered and scaled so the largest coordinate is\n`scale=`.\n\nSpring layouts are the general-purpose default: clusters pull together, bridges\nstretch between them and symmetric graphs tend to look symmetric. Each iteration costs\n`O(n^2)` (run in parallel on larger graphs), so use them up to a few thousand nodes.\nThis ports NetworkX's dense `spring_layout()` scheme (NetworkX switches to a different\nenergy-minimization method from 500 nodes; this method always uses the force\niteration). Edge direction is ignored and parallel edges add their weights. The same\n`seed=` always gives the same layout, though not the same one as NetworkX, whose\nrandom numbers differ.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[k]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Ideal distance between adjacent nodes. If `None` (default), uses `1/sqrt(n)`\n    (or the starting domain size over `sqrt(n)` when `fixed=` is given), which suits\n    the unit square the layout starts in. Larger values spread the nodes apart.\n\n<code>[iterations]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[50]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Maximum number of iterations. Default is `50`.\n\n<code>[threshold]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[0.0001]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Stop once the root-mean-square move per node falls below this. Default is `1e-4`.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[bool]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, use edge weights (`1` where missing) as spring strengths, so heavier\n    edges pull harder. If `False`, every edge counts `1`. If `None` (default),\n    follows whether the graph was created as weighted.\n\n<code>[initial]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Union[str, dict]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Starting positions, as the name of a node attribute holding `(x, y)` pairs or a\n    dict mapping node IDs or labels to pairs. Nodes without one start at random in a\n    square as large as the given positions. If `None` (default), all nodes start at\n    random in the unit square.\n\n<code>[fixed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[list]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node IDs or labels that keep their `initial=` positions. When given, the result\n    is not rescaled, so the fixed nodes stay where they are.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. `None` keeps the raw coordinates (`center=` is\n    then ignored). Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[seed]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Integer seed for the random starting positions. If `None` (default), the layout\n    differs on every call.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `k=` is not positive, `threshold=` is negative, a `fixed=` node has no\n    `initial=` position, an initial position is not a pair of finite numbers,\n    `weighted=True` and an edge weight is negative, or `scale=` or `center=` is\n    invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe two communities of the karate club pull apart:\n\n::: {#d1d28aad .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\n(\n    ec.karate_club()\n    .layout_spring(seed=1)\n    .plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"faction\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"position:relative;display:inline-block\">\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"600\" height=\"400\" viewBox=\"140.9 15.8 318.3 386.8\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"140.9\" y=\"15.8\" width=\"318.3\" height=\"386.8\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<line x1=\"319.0\" y1=\"285.0\" x2=\"306.7\" y2=\"271.6\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-1-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M320.9,283.5 C319.2,280.7 310.8,272.4 310.7,266.9 C310.6,261.3 318.6,253.1 320.2,250.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-2-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M336.2,213.2 C335.3,215.0 335.3,221.4 331.3,224.1 C327.3,226.7 316.8,224.7 312.1,229.2 C307.4,233.6 304.6,247.1 303.1,250.7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-1-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"336.7\" y1=\"213.5\" x2=\"331.0\" y2=\"227.7\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"0.96\" st